          {
            "id": 2787750,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Hello, and welcome. My name's Heather McCallum, and I'm one of the potters who work here at Edelman Pottery. Before we go into the workshop, I just want to say a bit about the craft of pottery. Then we'll have a look at the equipment, and you can try making a pot of your own. Like many people, I'm sure you know that pottery as an art form is tens of thousands of years old, and we know this because it stands the test of time.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2787751,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Hello, and welcome.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 76.075,
                  "from": 74.475,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787755,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "My name's Heather McCallum, and I'm one of the potters who work here at Edelman Pottery.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 83.56,
                  "from": 77.0,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787772,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Before we go into the workshop, I just want to say a bit about the craft of pottery.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 89.72,
                  "from": 84.12,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787791,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Then we'll have a look at the equipment, and you can try making a pot of your own.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 96.125,
                  "from": 90.365,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787810,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Like many people, I'm sure you know that pottery as an art form is tens of thousands of years old, and we know this because it stands the test of time.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 109.57,
                  "from": 96.924995,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2787841,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Things like baskets and pictures don't survive in the earth in the same way that pots do, and even if ancient pots are found in small pieces, they still provide a lot of information about the past. There's no doubt that pottery has given archaeologists a fascinating insight into how ancient humans lived. The shape of an artefact may have been lost, but archaeologists can tell whether the pots were for, say, storage or cooking by examining the impressions on the clay, the scratches from tools, and the clay itself can reveal where the pots came from. When I ask people why they want to take a pottery class with me, they sometimes talk about these things. Like our ancestors, they hope that something they create will also last longer than they do, that their work, whether it is good or not, might say something about humanity many years after their death.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2787842,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Things like baskets and pictures don't survive in the earth in the same way that pots do, and even if ancient pots are found in small pieces, they still provide a lot of information about the past.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 125.985,
                  "from": 110.21,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787880,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "There's no doubt that pottery has given archaeologists a fascinating insight into how ancient humans lived.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 136.03,
                  "from": 127.105,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787897,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The shape of an artefact may have been lost, but archaeologists can tell whether the pots were for, say, storage or cooking by examining the impressions on the clay, the scratches from tools, and the clay itself can reveal where the pots came from.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 157.13501,
                  "from": 136.67,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787940,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "When I ask people why they want to take a pottery class with me, they sometimes talk about these things.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 166.59001,
                  "from": 159.07,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2787961,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Like our ancestors, they hope that something they create will also last longer than they do, that their work, whether it is good or not, might say something about humanity many years after their death.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 184.005,
                  "from": 167.07,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2787997,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Of course, you will all have your own reasons for coming here. As far as I'm concerned, what I love most is the concentration you need to make a good pot. That focus takes you away from the stresses of everyday life. If you're elderly, it's also good exercise for hands and wrists and helps with arthritis, and of course it's a fun activity for children because it's so messy. Here at Edelman Pottery, we show you some of the basic pottery techniques so that you can use these to create whatever you wish, a gift for a friend perhaps.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2787998,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Of course, you will all have your own reasons for coming here.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 189.125,
